<DocsLayout title="Barcode API Authentication with API Keys | BarcodeNest" description="Authenticate BarcodeNest product lookup requests with the X-API-Key header and learn how to create, store, regenerate and revoke API keys." heading="Authenticate barcode API requests." intro="Use a BarcodeNest API key in the X-API-Key header for every product lookup request." current="authentication">
  <section><h2>Create your first API key</h2><ol class="docs-steps"><li><span>1</span><div><strong>Register</strong><p>Create a BarcodeNest account with email and password, Google, or GitHub.</p></div></li><li><span>2</span><div><strong>Complete onboarding</strong><p>The first API key is created automatically after registration.</p></div></li><li><span>3</span><div><strong>Copy and store the key</strong><p>The full secret is shown once. Store it in a password manager or secret-management service.</p></div></li><li><span>4</span><div><strong>Send a request</strong><p>Place the key in the <code class="inline-code">X-API-Key</code> request header.</p></div></li></ol></section>
  <section><h2>Request header</h2><CodeBlock label="Authenticated request" code={curl} language="bash" /><p>Do not place an API key in a query string, public client-side bundle, source repository, support message, or analytics event. Make product lookups from a trusted server whenever the application cannot protect a secret.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Key storage and lifecycle</h2><p>BarcodeNest stores only a cryptographic hash of the full API key. This design means the full secret cannot be displayed again after creation. The dashboard shows identifying key metadata rather than the reusable credential.</p><p>If a key is lost or exposed, regenerate it from the API Keys area. Regeneration creates a new secret and revokes the old credential. You can also revoke a key without creating a replacement.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Authentication errors</h2><p>A missing, invalid, revoked, or expired API key returns HTTP <code class="inline-code">401</code> with a structured error code. Authentication failures do not consume the monthly product lookup allowance.</p><p>Account sessions and developer API keys are separate credentials. Browser account routes use secure session cookies; the product lookup API uses <code class="inline-code">X-API-Key</code>. Continue with the <a href="/docs/barcode-lookup/">barcode lookup endpoint guide</a> or review all <a href="/docs/errors/">API errors</a>.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
